title: Fix bags-list on_idle benchmark fragility across MaxAutoRebagPerBlock values
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The benchmark failed depending on `MaxAutoRebagPerBlock` (e.g. it passes with 10 as configured in Westend, Polkadot and Kusama AH runtime but it failed with 5, as it was configured before, see [runtime PR](https://github.com/polkadot-fellows/runtimes/pull/1065)).

    Fix by placing all regular nodes in the lowest bag and setting scores for all pending nodes. This makes the count deterministic (only `on_idle` moves nodes into higher bags) and exercises worst-case weight (every node triggers a full rebag).
crates:
- name: pallet-bags-list
  bump: none
